in Dictionary,_חנן.1\" data-ref=\"Klein Dictionary, חנן 1\">חנן</a>.]", "parent_lexicon_details": {"name": "Klein Dictionary", "language": "heb.modern", "to_language": "eng", "text_categories": [], "source": "Klein Dictionary", "attribution": "Ezra Klein", "index_title": "Klein Dictionary", "version_title": "Carta Jerusalem; 1st edition, 1987", "version_lang": "en", "should_autocomplete": true}}, {"headword": "חַנּוּן", "parent_lexicon": "BDB Dictionary", "content": {"senses": [{"definition": "<strong>adj. gracious</strong>, only used as an attribute of God, as hearing the cry of the vexed debtor <a data-ref=\"Exodus 22:26\" href=\"/Exodus.22.26\">Ex 22:26</a> (covt. code), ‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">מְרַחֵם</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 116:5\" href=\"/Psalms.116.5\">ψ 116:5</a>; elsewhere in the earlier phrase <span dir=\"rtl\">רַחוּם וְחַנּוּן</span> <a data-ref=\"Exodus 34:6\" href=\"/Exodus.34.6\">Ex 34:6</a> (JE) = <a data-ref=\"Psalms 86:15\" href=\"/Psalms.86.15\">ψ 86:15</a>; <a data-ref=\"Psalms 103:8\" href=\"/Psalms.103.8\">103:8</a>, or the later <span dir=\"rtl\">חַנּוּן וְרַחוּם</span> <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 30:9\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.30.9\">2 Ch 30:9</a>; <a data-ref=\"Nehemiah 9:17\" href=\"/Nehemiah.9.17\">Ne 9:17</a>, <a data-ref=\"Nehemiah 9:31\" href=\"/Nehemiah.9.31\">31</a> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 111:4\" href=\"/Psalms.111.4\">ψ 111:4</a>; <a data-ref=\"Psalms 112:4\" href=\"/Psalms.112.4\">112:4</a>; <a data-ref=\"Psalms 145:8\" href=\"/Psalms.145.8\">145:8</a> <a data-ref=\"Joel 2:13\" href=\"/Joel.2.13\">Jo 2:13</a>; <a data-ref=\"Jonah 4:2\" href=\"/Jonah.4.2\">Jon 4:2</a>."}]}, "rid": "BDB03274", "strong_numbers": ["2587"], "next_hw": "חֲנִינָה", "prev_hw": "חָנוּן", "all_cited": true, "quotes": [], "GK": ["2843"], "TWOT": ["694d"], "parent_lexicon_details": {"name": "BDB Dictionary", "language": "heb.biblical", "to_language": "eng", "text_categories": [], "source": "BDB Dictionary", "attribution": "F. Brown, S. Driver & C. Briggs", "index_title": "BDB", "version_title": "A Hebrew and English lexicon of the Old Testament, by Francis Brown. With the co-operation of S. R. Driver and Charles A. Briggs. Oxford, 1906", "version_lang": "en", "should_autocomplete": true}}, {"headword": "חַנּוּן", "parent_lexicon": "Ben Yehuda Dictionary", "content": {"definition": ["<p>ת\"ז, —  שמדתו לַחֹן, barmherzig, gnädig; gracieux, miséricordieux; gracious, merciful:  והיה כי יצעק (העני) אלי ושמעתי כי חַנּוּן אני (<span class=\"by-source\">שמות כב כו</span>).  יי' יי' אל רחום וְחַנּוּן ארך אפים ורב חסד (<span class=\"by-source\">שם לד ו</span>).  ושובו אל יי' אלהיכם כי חַנּוּן ורחום הוא ארך אפים ורב חסד ונחם על הרעה (<span class=\"by-source\">יוא' ב יג</span>).  כי חַנּוּן  ורחום יי' אלהיכם ולא יסיר פנים מכם אם תשובו אליו (<span class=\"by-source\">דהי\"ב ל ט</span>).  כי אל חַנּוּן  ורחום אתה (<span class=\"by-source\">נחמ' ט לא</span>). חַנּוּן  יי' וצדיק ואלהינו מרחם (<span class=\"by-source\">תהל' קיו ה</span>).  — ובמשמ' שֵׁם: ברוך אתה יי' <strong>חנון</strong> המרבה לסלוח (<span class=\"by-source\">תפל' י\"ח, סלח</span>).  — ואמר הפיטן:  מפוזרת מקצה לקצה, חַנּוּן  סגוריה היְצא (<span class=\"by-source\">יוצ' שבת חוהמ\"פ, אלה</span>).</p>"]}, "rid": "BY-06406", "prev_hw": "חנוכה", "next_hw": "חִנּוּן", "page_num": 1648, "parent_lexicon_details": {"name": "Ben Yehuda Dictionary", "language": "heb", "to_language": "heb", "text_categories": [], "index_title": "Ben Yehuda Dictionary", "version_title": "Ben Yehuda Dictionary", "version_lang": "he", "should_autocomplete": true}}]